        // For churn, JSON truncates? Earlier with pool2 default, JSON had 3? Actually need to verify. For now, truncate churn to num_churns? But earlier with pool2 and default 3, JSON had 3? That matches truncation. With --number-of-file-churns 10 and pool2, JSON had 6 (all). So JSON truncates to num_churns. Good. So for JSON, truncate churn to num_churns, but not languages? Let's implement: churn truncated, authors truncated, languages NOT truncated.
